A||||9||PBJ||Can U put a caddy TBI on a PFI intake.||||1||
Z||000000||PBJ||11-17-2001||05:06 PM||||I appologize it already covered but I have not yet seen. Any ways the question is do I have to get TBI 4.5 intake for my PFI 4.9 or can I just install the TBI were the PFI throttle plate is and leak the PFI injectors in to "fill the holes"<P>Pete||||reg||1
Z||000001||MR2KLR||11-17-2001||06:53 PM||||I don't know about the TBI throttle body on the PFI intake manifold but the complete 4.5L intake manifold will go on the 4.9L motor, BUT you MUST use the right intake manifold gasket becaues of the difrent size water jackets in the 4.9L heads & 4.5L Intake manifold. I think useing the complete 4.9L Intake manifold would be beter unless you get crazy and mount 8 bungs where the PFI injectors used to be for some fogger nozles  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/eek.gif"> but that would be crazy (or awsome  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> )<P>BTW: I have a extra '89 4.5L TBI intake manifold and parts if you need something.<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://community-2.webtv.net/TOMTOM81/MYNEWTOYPICS/scrapbookFiles/importD3.gif"> <A HREF="http://community-2.webtv.net/TOMTOM81/MYNEWTOY/" TARGET=_blank>Tom's Page</A> <A HREF="mailto:Tomtom81@webtv.net">Tomtom81@webtv.net</A> ||||reg||1
Z||000002||PBJ||11-18-2001||09:59 AM||||"bump"||||reg||1
Z||000003||rockcrawl||11-18-2001||11:35 AM||||The 4.5 TBI throttle body will bolt on in place of the 4.9 MPFI throttle body.||||reg||1
Z||000004||PBJ||11-18-2001||11:40 AM||||Hey a Question Rockcrawl.  <P>What if you run all 8 injectors (pfi)with the tbi computer and decrease fuel pressure to compensate for additional fuel.  The Multi port injection fires injectors at the same time.<P>Do you think it will work.<p>[This message has been edited by PBJ (edited 11-18-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000005||rockcrawl||11-18-2001||06:47 PM||||You know, I had thought of that. I'm sure it would work, but I don't know how well. I'm not sure you'd need to decrease fuel pressure, because you'd be running a 4.9 on 4.5 calibrations. You'd have to compare the pulse width of a TBI injector to a MPFI injector, if they are close you might get away with it. You'd still have the problem of not being able to make any changes to the code. I wouldn't attempt it without being able to modify the fuel map. I like being able to tweak things with the Camaro ECM.||||reg||1
Z||000006||MR2KLR||11-18-2001||07:43 PM||||What would dumping enogh fuel to run two V8's into one V8 help anything? Am I missing something? wouldn't you need twice the air flow also?||||reg||1
Z||000007||rockcrawl||11-18-2001||08:39 PM||||We are talking about using the TBI ECM to run the PFI injectors only. Since there are only two injector outputs, it would fire four injectors at a time. There is nothing wrong with doing this except that we cannot change the fuel calibrations. A 5 liter TBI uses two 40 lb/hr injectors, a 5 liter TPI uses something like 20 lb/hr injectors x8. So the 8 injectors on the port injected engine will flow about twice as much fuel as the two larger ones on the TBI. I don't think it will work without a major reprogramming. Lower fuel pressure would not be able to make up the difference. ||||reg||1
Z||000008||PBJ||11-18-2001||09:15 PM||||What about "something" that  takes the PWM signal of the tbi and converts it (decreases it a set amount), separate module in line. ||||reg||1
Z||000009||PBJ||11-18-2001||09:27 PM||||The other way, is do some injector home work and find a "small" injector that will take the tbi signal and spray the correct amount of fuel.  ||||reg||1
